  "title": "Headless build in Brett's AmberX-AXF repo (worktree, branch claude/shots-tab).",
  "asked": "Headless build in Brett's AmberX-AXF repo (worktree, branch claude/shots-tab). Read CLAUDE.md + _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md. Opus, one session. Git auth is in your environment (GIT_CONFIG_*); just git push. Brett: UI Review (apps/console-web/plugins/ui-review) only shows PLANNED build screens waiting for approve/reject. There's no place for ad-hoc screenshots (a session checking a screen like the Breakroom, live captures, PR before/after, his own uploads). Add a **Screenshots** tab to UI Review: 1. Store: screenshots with {id, title, source (build|check|pr|manual|watch-live), session/build/agent, app, screen/route, viewport (phone/desktop), takenAt, before/after pair id, note}. Files on the console data volume; never enters the approve/reject queue. 2. Intake: server API (POST multipart/base64, console token or signed-in user) + CLI `node framework/cli/shot.mjs <file> --title --app --screen --source --session` + an Upload button in the tab (phone camera roll works). 3. UI: framework grid (sort/filter/search, date column), grouped by app / screen / source / day; thumbnails; tap -> full-screen viewer with swipe; before/after compare slider when paired; copy link; delete. Framework controls + theme/scale tokens only, compact. 4. 'Send to review' action promotes a shot into the normal approve/reject queue when wanted. 5. Migrate: any UI Review items titled 'Breakroom check:' (from a check session tonight) move into Screenshots. 6. Tell builds: add one line to the build brief template / RULES so check sessions use `axf shot` (not the review queue) for non-review screenshots. Tests (intake API auth, CLI, migration, never in review queue). Full local test block from .github/workflows/android.yml + theme/controls/lifecycle checks green. Commit, fetch+merge origin/main, retest, git push origin HEAD:main (retry until it lands). Report at _claude/builds/reports/shots-tab.md.",
